hat make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Present Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " The Present Continuous is formed like this:<br/><br/>Subject + the present tense of <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> + (main verb + <span class=\"italic\">ing</span>)<br/><br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I + am +  having</span> a few issues of my own.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>The Present Continuous", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Tense of To  Be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Verb + ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"am\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" having\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" having\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She/ He/ It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"is\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" having\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" having\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" having\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "How <span class=\"strong\">are</span> the renovations <span class=\"strong\">coming</span> along?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Now I<span class=\"strong\">'m having</span> a few issues of my own!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The rain <span class=\"strong\">is seeping</span> into the house because the shingles on the roof <span class=\"strong\">are peeling</span> off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">am trying</span> to figure out where this enormous gaping hole came from.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Are</span> you <span class=\"strong\">going</span> up the ladder?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Causative with Have and Get", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the causative with <span class=\"strong\">have</span> and <span class=\"strong\">get</span> to show that you want someone to do something for you.  You cause the person to do something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Causative Form with Have</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + agent + base form of the verb + object", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should have</span> a roofer <span class=\"strong\">look</span> at that right away!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/><span class=\"underline\">Causative Form with Get</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">get</span> + agent + infinitive + object", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">will definitely have to get</span> someone <span class=\"strong\">to repair</span> it.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you have the agent in the sentence we call it the ACTIVE causative.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">should have</span> a roofer <span class=\"strong\">look</span> at that right away!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">will</span> definitely <span class=\"strong\">have to get</span> someone <span class=\"strong\">to repair</span> it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">have to get</span> a professional <span class=\"strong\">to assess</span> what's happening here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We<span class=\"strong\">'ll get</span> Peter <span class=\"strong\">to help</span> us put it on the roof.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm afraid I can't stay right now because I<span class=\"strong\">'m having</span> Anna <span class=\"strong\">cut</span> my hair at 3. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bay window", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large window sticking out from an outside wall and forming an alcove in a room", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I got someone to put in a bay window in the front.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you fix a house.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shingles", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a roof covering consisting of individual overlapping elements", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rain is seeping into the house because the shingles on the roof are peeling off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "roof", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the external upper covering of a house or other building", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rain is seeping into the house because the shingles on the roof are peeling off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to peel off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to separate from a surface", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The shingles on the roof are peeling off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ladder", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a structure of wood, or metal, into which steps or rungs are set to provide a means of climbing up or down", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's get out the ladder and inspect the roof.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gaping", "type": "name"}, {"content": "wide, broad", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am trying to figure out where this enormous gaping hole came from.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hardware store", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a shop that sells tools for the house or garden ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are going to the hardware store to get a tarp.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tarp", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200blarge \u200bpiece of \u200bwaterproof \u200bcloth or \u200bplastic that is used as a \u200bcover", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are going to get a tarp for the roof.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"typ